  ],
  "description": "A revise must have exactly one target that is a begin or end act, and a content of a 7.6.6 form that, for a baseline act, equals the derivation and is not already the applicable content of an act, and that carries the target's policy when it revises an end act. An adopt_policy must name both policy and policy_version (both null adopting the baseline) and have exactly one target, a story's detection or an expectation. An end act naming a policy must target a begin act of a unit that policy governs. Each violation fails 10.2.9. @period on a review, policy keys of the wrong type in a detection's @frame, and policy keys on a review's @frame fail 10.2.4; an expectation context whose interpretation or policy has the wrong shape fails 10.2.3. A well-formed adopt_policy of the baseline is accepted.",
